And before you ask,


00:16:57.502 --> 00:16:59.374
I handcuffed myself
for tactical reasons


00:16:59.548 --> 00:17:01.289
that I do not have time
to explain.


00:17:01.463 --> 00:17:03.334
You shouldn'’t have gone off
on your own.


00:17:03.508 --> 00:17:05.206
We'’re supposed to be a team.


00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:07.599
Sorry, buddy.
I'’m still working on this teamwork thing.


00:17:07.773 --> 00:17:09.297
So now what?


00:17:09.471 --> 00:17:11.647
Well, I'’m not jumping
out of any more helicopters


00:17:11.821 --> 00:17:13.823
until we get some answers
from GUN.


00:17:13.997 --> 00:17:15.564
We need somewhere to regroup.


00:17:17.087 --> 00:17:18.915
I know just the place.


00:17:19.089 --> 00:17:21.483
["Lollipop"
by TEMPURA KIDZ playing]


00:17:27.097 --> 00:17:28.664
[all clapping]


00:17:29.447 --> 00:17:31.188
<i>Hai, chiizu.</i>[yelps]


00:17:31.362 --> 00:17:32.624
It'’s an ambush!


00:17:32.798 --> 00:17:34.800
You'’ll never take us alive,
foul beasts!


00:17:34.974 --> 00:17:37.325
Calm down, Knuckles.
This is a Chao Garden.


00:17:37.499 --> 00:17:40.589
One of the top ten must-see
spots in all of Tokyo!


00:17:40.763 --> 00:17:42.678
It'’s a perfect place
for us to blend in.


00:17:42.852 --> 00:17:44.506
Are you Detective Pikachu?


00:17:44.680 --> 00:17:46.116
Yes, he is!


00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:49.250
[chortles] He does
look like a Pokémon.


00:17:49.424 --> 00:17:50.381
"Pika, pika!" [laughs]


00:17:50.555 --> 00:17:52.340
Commander Walters!


00:17:52.514 --> 00:17:54.298
Sonic.


00:17:54.472 --> 00:17:57.214
Thank God you'’re all okay.
I'’m sure you have questions.


00:17:57.388 --> 00:18:00.087
Just a big ticked-off
red and black one.


00:18:00.261 --> 00:18:01.653
Who was that guy?


00:18:01.827 --> 00:18:04.526
Shadow'’s story
began a lot like yours, Sonic.


00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:07.485
But where you found family
and friends on this planet,


00:18:07.659 --> 00:18:11.185
Shadow found only pain and loss.


00:18:11.924 --> 00:18:14.275
<i>It begins over 50 years ago,</i>


00:18:14.449 --> 00:18:17.582
<i>with a meteor crash </i>
<i>in a quiet corner of Oklahoma.</i>


00:18:17.756 --> 00:18:21.369
<i>The meteorite contained</i>
<i>a life-form.</i>


00:18:24.111 --> 00:18:25.895
<i>The ultimate life-form.</i>


00:18:27.897 --> 00:18:30.378
<i>Shadow'’s power--</i>
<i>his "chaos energy"--</i>


00:18:30.552 --> 00:18:33.555
<i>went far beyond</i>
<i>any living creature.</i>


00:18:36.166 --> 00:18:38.734
<i>The scientist</i>
<i>who discovered him</i> <i>believed this power</i>


00:18:38.908 --> 00:18:41.084
<i>would usher in a new era</i>
<i>for humanity.</i>


00:18:42.607 --> 00:18:45.741
<i>But Shadow'’s power</i>
<i>proved too dangerous.</i>


00:18:48.657 --> 00:18:50.659
<i>A terrible accident</i>
<i>destroyed the lab,</i>


00:18:50.833 --> 00:18:53.096
<i>taking human lives with it.</i>[siren wailing]


00:18:53.270 --> 00:18:57.535
<i>The project leader</i>
<i>was blamed for the incident</i> <i>and imprisoned.</i>


00:18:57.709 --> 00:18:59.363
<i>With the program canceled...</i>[yelps in pain]


00:18:59.537 --> 00:19:02.497
<i>...Shadow was a loose end </i>
<i>no one knew how to deal with.</i>


00:19:03.759 --> 00:19:05.674
<i>Too dangerous</i>
<i>to be walking free,</i>


00:19:05.848 --> 00:19:08.198
<i>too valuable to destroy.</i>


00:19:09.286 --> 00:19:11.462
<i>So I had him placed</i>
<i>into stasis...</i>


00:19:14.161 --> 00:19:16.163
<i>indefinitely.</i>


00:19:18.165 --> 00:19:21.255
Wait a second. If Shadow'’s
been on ice for 50 years,


00:19:21.429 --> 00:19:23.692
someone had to help him escape.True.


00:19:23.866 --> 00:19:25.520
But there'’s only a few people
in the world


00:19:25.694 --> 00:19:27.565
who even know
of Shadow'’s existence.


00:19:34.659 --> 00:19:37.532
[J-pop cover of
"I Want You Back" by Jackson 5 playing]


00:19:37.706 --> 00:19:39.882
[people cheering]


00:19:43.668 --> 00:19:46.105
A live show? Yeah!


00:19:49.848 --> 00:19:51.850
[drones humming]


00:19:55.419 --> 00:19:56.420
Get down!


00:20:02.426 --> 00:20:05.603
[people screaming]


00:20:06.778 --> 00:20:08.650
[groaning]


00:20:11.130 --> 00:20:12.393
Egg drones?


00:20:12.567 --> 00:20:15.265
But Robotnik
is supposed to be dead!


00:20:26.058 --> 00:20:28.322
Konnichi-what?


00:20:30.367 --> 00:20:31.586
[weapons powering up]


00:20:31.760 --> 00:20:33.501
[motorbike revving]


00:20:42.118 --> 00:20:43.772
[tires squeal]


00:20:49.256 --> 00:20:53.347
I'’m sorry, we already had
our big motorcycle chase for the evening.


00:20:58.003 --> 00:20:58.961
Commander Walters!


00:20:59.135 --> 00:21:00.397
[Knuckles grunts]


00:21:00.571 --> 00:21:02.617
[Sonic] Commander Walters,
are you okay?


00:21:03.792 --> 00:21:04.793
Sonic...


00:21:04.967 --> 00:21:06.229
[painful grunt]


00:21:07.404 --> 00:21:08.536
...take this.


00:21:08.710 --> 00:21:10.755
[Sonic] What is it?[Walters] A key...


00:21:11.974 --> 00:21:14.542
to the most powerful weapon
GUN has ever built.


00:21:14.716 --> 00:21:17.240
You'’re the only one I trust
to keep it safe.


00:21:17.414 --> 00:21:19.111
[exhales weakly]


00:21:19.286 --> 00:21:20.591
Commander Walters...


00:21:20.765 --> 00:21:22.289
[sirens, vehicles approaching][gasps]


00:21:26.597 --> 00:21:28.251
[indistinct shouts]


00:21:29.426 --> 00:21:30.906
Alpha team, fan out!


00:21:32.299 --> 00:21:33.691
Do we have eyes?


00:21:34.344 --> 00:21:35.345
Secure the perimeter!


00:21:38.653 --> 00:21:40.002
Medevac is en route.


00:21:40.176 --> 00:21:41.830
[indistinct radio chatter]


00:21:43.832 --> 00:21:45.312
His launch key is missing.


00:21:52.536 --> 00:21:54.756
I knew they couldn'’t be trusted.


00:21:57.019 --> 00:21:58.629
[all exclaiming]


00:21:58.803 --> 00:22:00.239
[Tails] Why are we
running from GUN?


00:22:00.414 --> 00:22:01.893
Aren'’t we on the same team?


00:22:02.067 --> 00:22:03.330
[Sonic] Until we get
more information,


00:22:03.504 --> 00:22:05.201
we'’re not trusting anyone.


00:22:05.375 --> 00:22:07.072
Follow me.Get it... off!


00:22:24.786 --> 00:22:26.788
Hold it right there,
Tokyo Drift!


00:22:26.962 --> 00:22:28.355
Who are you?


00:22:31.227 --> 00:22:33.577
[gasps] It'’s the Goat Milker!


00:22:33.751 --> 00:22:36.014
[mimicking Knuckles]
"It'’s the Goat Milker!"


00:22:36.188 --> 00:22:38.234
Relax.
I'’m not here to fight.


00:22:38.408 --> 00:22:41.455
Then why are you here?And why did you free Shadow?


00:22:41.629 --> 00:22:43.544
Are you kidding?


00:22:43.718 --> 00:22:47.330
The last thing we want
is more super-powered hedgehogs running around.


00:22:47.504 --> 00:22:49.463
The doctor had nothing
to do with it.


00:22:51.160 --> 00:22:52.988
And I can prove it.[car alarm chirps]


00:23:08.395 --> 00:23:10.005
Please,


00:23:10.179 --> 00:23:11.223
join me in the crab.


00:23:12.790 --> 00:23:15.967
[narrator] <i>And now back to... </i>
<i>"La UÚltima Pasión."</i>


00:23:16.141 --> 00:23:17.839
I have fallen in love
with another.


00:23:18.013 --> 00:23:19.797
[gasps]


00:23:19.971 --> 00:23:23.235
But who, Gabriella?
Tell me who!


00:23:25.063 --> 00:23:27.196
My twin brother, Pablo?


00:23:28.415 --> 00:23:29.851
<i>Pablo!</i>


00:23:31.766 --> 00:23:33.158
!¡Bastardo!


00:23:33.332 --> 00:23:35.726
Buenos días, !¡hermano!


00:23:35.900 --> 00:23:37.032
<i>No!</i>


00:23:37.206 --> 00:23:39.338
[cackling]


00:23:39.513 --> 00:23:41.819
Let that be a lesson
to you, Juan.


00:23:41.993 --> 00:23:43.560
[beeping]Family


00:23:43.734 --> 00:23:46.955
is a field
of emotional claymores


00:23:47.129 --> 00:23:49.348
that leave you abandoned,
betrayed


00:23:51.133 --> 00:23:54.005
and weeping
while you eat cake,


00:23:54.179 --> 00:23:56.573
which creates copious amounts
of adipose tissue,


00:23:56.747 --> 00:23:59.750
and what some calloused
individuals refer to as...


00:23:59.924 --> 00:24:02.536
[sniffs deeply]
...man boobs.


00:24:02.710 --> 00:24:03.885
Ha.


00:24:05.800 --> 00:24:08.063
[up-tempo Latin jazz playing]


00:24:13.242 --> 00:24:14.852
[slapping along
with the congas]


00:24:17.420 --> 00:24:18.987
[trilling loudly]


00:24:20.118 --> 00:24:21.511
[shrieking]


00:24:21.685 --> 00:24:23.731
Doctor,
we have visitors.


00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:27.212
Really?


00:24:27.386 --> 00:24:30.085
I thought I was having
an anthropomorphic nightmare.


00:24:30.259 --> 00:24:31.739
Where the only person
I could trust in the world


00:24:31.913 --> 00:24:33.436
showed up with
all my worst enemies,


00:24:33.610 --> 00:24:35.307
while I was in a bathrobe,


00:24:35.482 --> 00:24:37.745
playing congas
on my big, fat belly!


00:24:37.919 --> 00:24:39.181
Sorry, sir.


00:24:39.355 --> 00:24:41.488
I don'’t believe it.
Eggman'’s alive?


00:24:41.662 --> 00:24:44.012
And he'’s never
looked worse.


00:24:44.186 --> 00:24:46.493
[cackling] Well, maybe,


00:24:46.667 --> 00:24:50.540
this is what not giving a damn
what you think I look like looks like.


00:24:50.714 --> 00:24:53.935
Sir, right now we have
an even bigger problem.


00:24:54.109 --> 00:24:55.502
Oh, come on.


00:24:57.634 --> 00:24:59.941
There'’s an imposter out there
using your technology.


00:25:00.115 --> 00:25:03.422
Imposter.
That'’s impossi-- What?


00:25:03.597 --> 00:25:05.076
No.


00:25:05.250 --> 00:25:09.298
My sweet mechanized spawn!


00:25:09.472 --> 00:25:13.084
Whomever this party-pooping
posse is looking for


00:25:13.258 --> 00:25:15.565
has stolen my persona


00:25:15.739 --> 00:25:19.090
and the precious babies
from my egg sac.


00:25:19.787 --> 00:25:21.266
Well...


00:25:21.440 --> 00:25:25.836
I'’ll soon egg-xact
my revenge.


00:25:26.010 --> 00:25:27.664
You see what I did there?[chuckles]


00:25:27.838 --> 00:25:31.059
It'’s time for the dramatic
soap-opera twist,


00:25:31.233 --> 00:25:35.367
where this Pablo
reveals his Juan!


00:25:35.542 --> 00:25:39.415
By cross-referencing
the precise coordinates


00:25:39.589 --> 00:25:42.331
of each drone'’s
energy spikes,


00:25:43.071 --> 00:25:45.203
I can track my babies


00:25:45.377 --> 00:25:47.989
to the imposter'’s
base of operations,


00:25:48.163 --> 00:25:49.556
right about...


00:25:49.730 --> 00:25:50.557
there!


00:25:50.731 --> 00:25:52.471
Sonic, I hate to say it,


00:25:52.646 --> 00:25:54.822
but I think we'’re both
after the same person.


00:25:54.996 --> 00:25:57.433
Hold on, hold on.
You'’re not suggesting we team up


00:25:57.607 --> 00:25:59.914
with Doctor Ro-Butt-Stink,
are you?


00:26:00.088 --> 00:26:01.524
Perhaps the fox is right.


00:26:01.698 --> 00:26:04.571
It could be our only chance
to find this mysterious,


00:26:04.745 --> 00:26:06.137
more impressive hedgehog.


00:26:06.311 --> 00:26:07.486
[groans]


00:26:07.661 --> 00:26:09.706
All right, Egghead.
I hate to say it,


00:26:09.880 --> 00:26:11.447
but it looks like
we'’re partners.


00:26:12.579 --> 00:26:14.493
On one condition.


00:26:15.973 --> 00:26:18.541
Dude, you have serious issues.


00:26:18.715 --> 00:26:19.803
Ow!


00:26:22.023 --> 00:26:23.459
[gibbering spasm]


00:26:23.633 --> 00:26:24.808
Let'’s...


00:26:25.592 --> 00:26:26.723
do this!


00:26:26.897 --> 00:26:28.595
["Firestarter"
by The Prodigy playing]


00:26:35.340 --> 00:26:36.472
[pained groan]


00:26:50.007 --> 00:26:51.922
[door thuds][Robotnik grunting]


00:26:53.097 --> 00:26:54.316
Suck it in!


00:26:54.490 --> 00:26:55.665
[grunting][door rattling]


00:26:56.840 --> 00:26:58.189
Tinker-tailor?


00:26:58.363 --> 00:26:59.800
I need room.


00:26:59.974 --> 00:27:02.629
Think Elvis, circa 1976.


00:27:02.803 --> 00:27:05.066
But sir, I don'’t have
the proper materials.


00:27:06.110 --> 00:27:07.459
Found some.


00:27:09.984 --> 00:27:11.159
Resourceful.


00:27:13.596 --> 00:27:15.511
[thunder rumbling]


00:27:39.013 --> 00:27:41.015
[faint, indistinct chatter]


00:27:51.678 --> 00:27:53.767
Hey! This is a restricted area.


00:27:53.941 --> 00:27:56.204
Oh, it'’s okay.
She'’s the professor'’s granddaughter.


00:27:56.378 --> 00:27:58.510
He takes her everywhere.


00:27:58.685 --> 00:28:01.775
Welcome to the lab, Maria.
I'’m Captain Walters.


00:28:01.949 --> 00:28:03.341
Oh, do you know
where my room is?


00:28:03.515 --> 00:28:05.082
Yeah, down the hall
and to the right.


00:28:05.256 --> 00:28:06.780
Make yourself at home.


00:28:06.954 --> 00:28:08.129
But, um,


00:28:08.303 --> 00:28:10.087
let'’s lose the skates,
okay, kiddo?


00:28:10.261 --> 00:28:11.698
Okay.


00:28:16.615 --> 00:28:19.096
[machinery humming softly]


00:28:32.588 --> 00:28:34.721
[fluid bubbling faintly]


00:28:48.082 --> 00:28:49.561
[light chuckle]


00:28:57.526 --> 00:28:58.570
[chuckles]


00:28:59.920 --> 00:29:01.660
[bag rustling]


00:29:03.662 --> 00:29:04.925
[pen uncaps]


00:29:21.376 --> 00:29:22.681
[laughs]


00:29:43.224 --> 00:29:46.096
["End of the Line"
by the Traveling Wilburys playing]


00:30:11.295 --> 00:30:12.470
[delighted shriek]


00:30:12.644 --> 00:30:14.472
[squealing]


00:30:22.176 --> 00:30:23.003
[gasps]


00:30:23.177 --> 00:30:24.134
[yelling]


00:30:28.922 --> 00:30:30.097
[whooping]


00:30:31.925 --> 00:30:33.100
Look out!


00:30:34.666 --> 00:30:35.842
[crashing]


00:30:52.336 --> 00:30:53.772
[faint roaring]


00:31:11.486 --> 00:31:13.662
[song ends]


00:31:13.836 --> 00:31:15.925
[crickets chirping softly]


00:31:17.013 --> 00:31:18.188
Wow.


00:31:18.885 --> 00:31:20.321
Look at all those stars.


00:31:22.149 --> 00:31:23.977
They'’re like diamonds.


00:31:25.674 --> 00:31:27.415
My grandfather says


00:31:27.589 --> 00:31:29.243
it can take hundreds of years


00:31:29.417 --> 00:31:31.419
for the light of a star
to reach Earth.


00:31:32.159 --> 00:31:34.030
And by the time you see it,


00:31:34.204 --> 00:31:36.511
the star might not even
exist anymore.


00:31:38.034 --> 00:31:39.514
Isn'’t that crazy?


00:31:40.994 --> 00:31:42.865
A light shines,


00:31:43.039 --> 00:31:44.998
even though the star is gone.


00:31:46.564 --> 00:31:48.392
Yeah, it does.


00:31:50.220 --> 00:31:51.918
I wonder which one
you came from, Shadow.


00:31:52.092 --> 00:31:52.962
I don'’t know.


00:31:54.094 --> 00:31:56.574
I don'’t know anything
about my home.


00:31:56.748 --> 00:31:59.142
This is your home, Shadow.


00:31:59.882 --> 00:32:01.014
Earth.


00:32:07.934 --> 00:32:09.239
Maria,


00:32:09.892 --> 00:32:11.589
do you think I'’m...


00:32:12.547 --> 00:32:13.809
dangerous?


00:32:15.071 --> 00:32:16.899
What are you talking about?


00:32:17.073 --> 00:32:19.641
The way the scientists
look at me,


00:32:19.815 --> 00:32:21.512
I can tell they'’re afraid.


00:32:21.686 --> 00:32:25.255
Like I'’m the horrible thing
from that movie we watched.


00:32:26.343 --> 00:32:27.779
I don'’t know...


00:32:28.476 --> 00:32:29.956
what I am.


00:32:35.222 --> 00:32:36.788
You'’re my friend.


00:32:38.138 --> 00:32:40.792
And you can do or be
anything you want.


00:32:41.968 --> 00:32:43.578
Not because of your powers,


00:32:43.752 --> 00:32:47.190
but because of who you are...
in here.


00:32:50.019 --> 00:32:52.195
I don'’t know what I'’d do
without you.


00:33:01.988 --> 00:33:04.991
["End of the Line" resumes]


00:33:09.473 --> 00:33:11.171
[song ends abruptly]


00:33:11.345 --> 00:33:12.999
[dust crackling]


00:33:29.841 --> 00:33:31.452
[footfalls]


00:33:34.107 --> 00:33:35.804
Professor?


00:33:35.978 --> 00:33:39.025
It'’s good to see you,
Shadow.


00:33:39.199 --> 00:33:41.288
I knew you'’d come home.


00:33:41.462 --> 00:33:44.030
I can'’t get her out of my head.


00:33:44.204 --> 00:33:45.727
The pain...


00:33:45.901 --> 00:33:47.250
It'’s too much.


00:33:47.424 --> 00:33:50.906
And that is why
we have to punish them.


00:33:55.432 --> 00:33:57.043
Okay, I don'’t like you
and you don'’t like me.


00:33:57.217 --> 00:33:59.045
Let'’s get this
over with quickly.


00:33:59.219 --> 00:34:01.047
Out of my way, dorkupine.


00:34:01.221 --> 00:34:03.310
"Dorkupine"?
Really clever.


00:34:07.749 --> 00:34:09.620
[hollow tapping]


00:34:09.794 --> 00:34:11.883
This door is six-inch-thick
solid steel


00:34:12.058 --> 00:34:13.842
on a pressurized latch.


00:34:14.016 --> 00:34:16.192
I'’ll need a moment to calculate
the molecular density


00:34:16.366 --> 00:34:17.976
and invert
the venting mechanics.


00:34:18.151 --> 00:34:19.587
[thunderous crash]


00:34:21.632 --> 00:34:22.894
[Knuckles] I unlocked it.


00:34:23.069 --> 00:34:26.072
[Robotnik] Subtle as always,
fist-for-brains.


00:34:27.334 --> 00:34:29.075
Easy, Shadow.


00:34:29.249 --> 00:34:31.729
Those are the guests
I'’ve been expecting.


00:34:31.903 --> 00:34:34.558
Let'’s give them
a warm welcome.


00:34:38.388 --> 00:34:39.737
[Stone] Whoa.


00:34:39.911 --> 00:34:41.174
What is this place?


00:34:41.348 --> 00:34:43.306
[Sonic] It looks like
a military base,


00:34:43.480 --> 00:34:45.308
but nobody'’s been here
for years.


00:34:45.482 --> 00:34:46.875
I wonder if it'’s haunted.


00:34:47.049 --> 00:34:49.965
Haunted? Nobody said anything
about being haunted.


00:34:50.139 --> 00:34:53.099
What'’s the matter?
You afraid of g-g-g-ghosts?


00:34:53.273 --> 00:34:55.362
Nothing scares
an Echidna warrior.


00:34:55.536 --> 00:34:57.929
Uh, yeah. Do you remember
what happened last movie night?


00:34:58.104 --> 00:34:59.670
[screaming in terror]


00:34:59.844 --> 00:35:01.150
[piercing scream][all yelling]


00:35:01.324 --> 00:35:02.760
Let go, let go, let go!


00:35:02.934 --> 00:35:05.633
There is no such thing
as a friendly ghost.


00:35:07.200 --> 00:35:08.723
[Sonic]
So which way do we go?


00:35:08.897 --> 00:35:12.596
I know! We should split up.


00:35:12.770 --> 00:35:15.991
Everyone with hideous,
brightly-colored fur take the left and the middle.


00:35:16.165 --> 00:35:17.775
Stone and I will go right.


00:35:17.949 --> 00:35:19.690
No, no, no, no, no. I'’m not
letting you out of my sight.


00:35:19.864 --> 00:35:21.649
Tails, you and Stone go left.


00:35:21.823 --> 00:35:24.913
Knuckles, you take the middle.
Eggman, you and me go right.


00:35:25.087 --> 00:35:27.002
By all means.


00:35:27.176 --> 00:35:28.656
We could use some
time together.


00:35:28.830 --> 00:35:30.440
To work on
your trust issues.


00:35:30.614 --> 00:35:33.443
You know what? You'’re right.
I should be more trusting.


00:35:33.617 --> 00:35:36.403
I mean, you'’ve only tried
to kill me twice!


00:35:38.448 --> 00:35:40.668
Just a dark, creepy hallway.


00:35:40.842 --> 00:35:42.539
Nothing to be afraid of.


00:35:44.280 --> 00:35:45.977
You hear that, ghost?


00:35:46.152 --> 00:35:47.675
You don'’t frighten me!


00:35:47.849 --> 00:35:49.416
[steam hissing][yells]


00:35:52.158 --> 00:35:54.551
Get... a... grip.


00:35:55.465 --> 00:35:57.206
Boo.[screams]


00:35:59.904 --> 00:36:02.603
I'’m just gonna
come right out and say this:


00:36:02.777 --> 00:36:05.562
You'’re adorable.[chuckles]
Oh, um, thanks.


00:36:05.736 --> 00:36:09.175
So, what'’s it like
being Sonic'’s assistant?


00:36:09.349 --> 00:36:12.656
You have a daily routine?
Paid time off? Benefits?


00:36:12.830 --> 00:36:16.007
Oh, I'’m not Sonic'’s assistant.
We'’re teammates.


00:36:16.182 --> 00:36:18.184
He'’s the leader,
Knuckles is the muscle,


00:36:18.358 --> 00:36:19.924
and I'’m the gadget guy.


00:36:20.098 --> 00:36:21.448
We all have a role to play.


00:36:21.622 --> 00:36:23.363
That'’s what makes the team
so special!


00:36:23.537 --> 00:36:25.278
That and the fact
we'’re best friends.


00:36:26.017 --> 00:36:27.323
You are?


00:36:27.497 --> 00:36:29.325
Well, yeah.
Just like you and Eggman, right?


00:36:31.153 --> 00:36:33.199
Uh... Yeah, eh...


00:36:33.373 --> 00:36:35.375
Of course! Yes.


00:36:35.549 --> 00:36:38.421
Me and the doctor,
best of friends.


00:36:39.901 --> 00:36:41.468
That'’s definitely
what we are.


00:36:41.642 --> 00:36:43.774
[metallic clattering]


00:36:43.948 --> 00:36:45.733
[squeaking]


00:36:46.690 --> 00:36:47.735
Hmm.


00:36:52.740 --> 00:36:54.481
[both screaming]


00:37:06.841 --> 00:37:10.410
Whoa. Look at all this stuff.


00:37:10.584 --> 00:37:13.717
This was more than
just a military base or a lab.


00:37:14.283 --> 00:37:15.719
It was a home.


00:37:15.893 --> 00:37:17.460
People lived here.


00:37:18.069 --> 00:37:19.549
He had a family.


00:37:20.289 --> 00:37:22.117
Is that what I smell?


00:37:22.291 --> 00:37:25.381
The stench
of domestic harmony?


00:37:25.555 --> 00:37:29.080
You ever wonder what
your life would have been like if you had a family?


00:37:29.255 --> 00:37:30.691
Hmm... No!


00:37:30.865 --> 00:37:32.867
Maybe you wouldn'’t have gone
full supervillain.


00:37:33.041 --> 00:37:35.870
I have no parents,
no aunts, no uncles.


00:37:36.044 --> 00:37:38.568
And something about my attitude
renders me...


00:37:39.526 --> 00:37:43.660
undesirable
to all possible genders.


00:37:45.532 --> 00:37:47.708
My future is a cul-de-sac!


00:37:48.709 --> 00:37:50.711
The Robotnik name ends...


00:37:52.365 --> 00:37:54.018
<i>avec moi.</i>


00:37:54.192 --> 00:37:56.238
Yes, I know French.


00:37:57.283 --> 00:37:58.762
[shuddering spasm]


00:38:00.764 --> 00:38:01.852
Whoa.


00:38:02.026 --> 00:38:05.029
Is this where you grew up,
Shadow?


00:38:05.203 --> 00:38:06.988
No wonder you'’re so mad.


00:38:07.162 --> 00:38:10.034
